      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Woodlands Regional Bus Interchange was Singapore's first underground bus interchange, built beneath the Woodlands MRT station.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Woodlands%2C_Singapore",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The Johor‑Singapore Causeway opened in 1923, marking the first permanent road link that brought Woodlands into the national transport network.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        21
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Woodlands%2C_Singapore",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Woodlands New Town emerged in the 1980s as part of Singapore's decentralisation plan, creating a self‑contained residential area with its own HDB flats.",
